                "ImageDescription": {
                  "value": "<div class=\"description\">\nScholars and enthusiasts alike believe this portrait of Abraham Lincoln, taken on November 8, 1863, eleven days before his famed Gettysburg Address, to be the best photograph of him ever taken. Lincoln\u2019s character was notoriously difficult to capture in pictures, but Alexander Gardner\u2019s close-up portrait, quite innovative in contrast to the typical full-length portrait style, comes closest to preserving the expressive contours of Lincoln\u2019s face and his penetrating gaze. Photograph taken by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Gardner_(photographer)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Alexander Gardner (photographer)\">Alexander Gardner</a>, 1863.</div>",
                  "source": "commons-desc-page"
